# The annotator (@bpartners/roof-analyser 0.17.0+) takes ONE credential — the signed-in Cognito token —
# and routes every call it makes through the Dashboard API named by REACT_APP_BPARTNERS_API_URL: the
# records, the geocoder (/geodata/geocode), the imagery tiles (/geoserver/wms), the roof detection, the 3D
# generation and the LLM report, all on Authorization: Bearer. Nothing else is configured for it, and
# nothing has to be proxied: the bridge answers CORS, which is what the old same-origin WMS proxy
# (REACT_APP_WMS_TILE_BASE_URL / GEOSERVER_ORIGIN) existed to work around. The GeoData lambda keys
# (REACT_APP_GEODATA_API_URL / _API_KEY, and the older REACT_APP_WMS_RESOLVER*) are no longer read at all.
# Meters added on every side of the traced roof before asking for the 3D model. Blank keeps the library's
# default (2 m); 0 sends the roof as traced.
REACT_APP_ROOF_MODEL_MARGIN_M=
# Debug knobs on the generated roof cleanup. Blank keeps the library's defaults.
# Meters within which two generated roof corners are merged into one (default 0.5 m); 0 turns snapping off.
REACT_APP_ROOF_SNAP_TOLERANCE_M=
# Meters a generated roof corner may sit off its ring's path and still be dropped (default 0.5 m); 0 turns it off.
REACT_APP_ROOF_SIMPLIFY_TOLERANCE_M=
# true/false: once the analysis or the 3D generation has run, close the 2D tab for good — the emprise they
# answer for stops being retraceable. Blank keeps the library's default (false), every tab reachable.
REACT_APP_ROOF_DISABLE_SWITCH_BACK=
# true/false: pre-fill a fresh visit's emprise from the backend's building footprint, and only ever in
# roofer mode. Blank keeps the library's default (true).
REACT_APP_ROOF_AUTO_DETECT_FOOTPRINT=
# true/false: the roofer's guided walk. Blank keeps the library's default (false); its Terminer button
# also needs an onFinish, which the annotator screen does not pass.
REACT_APP_ROOF_ROOFER_BUTTON_MODE=
# true/false: leave the 3D tab as the generation's read-out — the model turns and a pan can still be
# picked and renamed, but no measuring bar, no cotes, no pente and no saved measures; the sidebar and the
# exported PDF carry the roof's total surface and each pan's own, nothing more. Blank keeps the library's
# default (false). Says nothing in roofer mode, which drops the 3D tab altogether.
REACT_APP_ROOF_SHOW_3D_RESULT_ONLY=
